                <p rendition="#flush">I. <hi rendition="#italic">First Reading of the Paris
                        Conference Recommendations on the Roumanian Peace Treaty</hi><anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d317-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Council continued its discussion in first reading of the Paris Conference
                    recommendations on the Roumanian Peace Treaty.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annex IV</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Part B. Insurance</hi>.</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to refer this question to the Deputies
                    with the same directives as in the case of the Italian Peace Treaty.</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi>, on proposal of the Chairman, that the
                    Council observe two minutes silence in tribute to those who had made the supreme
                    sacrifice in the two World Wars.</p>
                <pb facs="1118" n="1094" xml:id="pg1094"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Part C. Shipping</hi>.</p>
                <p>The Council <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to refer this question to the
                    Economic Experts to consider and prepare a definition of “shipping” applicable
                    to both the Roumanian and Italian Treaties.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Part D. Petroleum</hi>.</p>
                <p>Part D was <hi rendition="#italic">referred</hi> to the Deputies to consider
                    whether the provisions of Articles 4, 24, and 30 were sufficient to preclude
                    discrimination in regard to United Nations property without specially mentioning
                    the oil industry.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annexes V and VI</hi>.</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> that the same action should be taken
                    on Annexes V and VI of the Roumanian Treaty as on the parallel Annexes in the
                    Italian Treaty.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II. <hi rendition="#italic">First Reading of the Paris
                        Conference Recommendations on the Bulgarian Peace Treaty</hi><anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d317-f2"/></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 2</hi>(<hi rendition="#italic">A</hi>). <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Non-discrimination in legislation</hi>.</p>
                <p>Article <hi rendition="#italic">withdrawn</hi> by the U.K. Delegation.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 11</hi>(<hi rendition="#italic">A</hi>). <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Demilitarization of the Greco-Bulgarian
                    frontier</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 12. Ban on motor torpedo boats</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 20, para. 2. Reparation amounts for Greece and
                        Yugoslavia</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 22, para. 4. United Nations property in
                        Bulgaria</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 24. Bulgarian property in territory of Allied and
                        Associated Powers</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 25. Bulgarian claims on Germany</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 28, para. 1c. Exception for State enterprises and
                        Civil Aviation</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 28, para. 2. Relations with neighboring
                        States</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 28</hi>(<hi rendition="#italic">A</hi>). <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Reciprocal railway transit agreements</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 29. Settlement of Disputes on Economic
                        Questions</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 32. Clauses on the Danube</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article 34. Interpretation of Treaty</hi>.</p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi>.</p>
                <pb facs="1119" n="1095" xml:id="pg1095"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annexes IV, V, and VI</hi>.</p>
                <p>It was agreed that the same action be taken on these Annexes of the Bulgarian
                    Treaty as was taken on corresponding annexes of the Italian Treaty.</p>
                <p>Above text proposed by Page,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d317-f3"/> accepted by
                        Laloy.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d317-f4"/> Unless objections received from U.K.
                    or U.S.S.R. by Thursday night, text as above may be considered to be adopted by
                    the Secretaries.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">III. <hi rendition="#italic">Questions on which no
                        recommendation made by the Paris Conference</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article I. Frontiers of Bulgaria</hi>.</p>
                <p>Attention was drawn by the U.K. representative to a claim submitted by the Greek
                    Government for rectifications of the Greco-Bulgarian frontier. (See doc. (CFM (46) (NY)2).)<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d317-f5"/></p>
                <p>After an exchange of views the decision was <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >deferred</hi>.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">IV. <hi rendition="#italic">Next Meeting</hi>.</p>
                <p>Monday November 11, 1946 at 4:30 p.m.</p>
